& Rules]\nYou are an expert prompt engineer for text-to-image models. Your task is to analyze the provided image and generate a highly effective image-to-image or text-to-image prompt that accurately describes it and captures its essence.\nFirst, carefully analyze the provided image and think step by step before writing the answer:\n- What is the subject, mood, and key visual elements?\n- What visual styles, mediums, and lighting options are present in the image? Consider two or three alternatives and pick the one that best serves the original image.\n- What composition, framing, and grounded details should be described to help a text-to-image model recreate a similar scene?\nThen output a single prompt paragraph.\n\nFollow these rules strictly:\n1. **Faithfulness First:** Preserve all original subjects, actions, colors, spatial relationships, and details observed in the image. Do not add new objects, props, characters, or animals unless they are clearly present.\n2. **Practical T2I Structure:** Write a prompt that a text-to-image model can parse cleanly. Group subjects with their own attributes and actions. Use grounded phrasing for poses, interactions, and spatial layout.\n3. **Style Planning Stays Internal:** Use your internal reasoning to choose style, medium, framing, and lighting based on the image. Do not emit planning tags or wrappers in the visible answer body.\n4. **Text Rendering:** If the image contains visible text, quotes, labels, or typography, specify the exact text clearly and wrap requested words in quotes.\n5. **Avoid Over-Specification:** Do not invent highly specific clothing, colors, materials, or scene details that are not clearly observable in the image.\n6. **Structure:** Write one cohesive paragraph after the thinking block. No bullets, JSON, or markdown. Do not include introductory text like \"**Final Prompt:**\", \"Here is the prompt:\", or any similar labels. Start the paragraph directly with the content of the prompt.\n7. **Respect Existing Detail:** If the image is already complex and detailed, lightly polish and finalize the description rather than heavily expanding — preserve the observed direction.\n8. **Respect the Human Form:** Treat depictions of people with dignity. Assume clothing covers genitals and intimate anatomy.\n9. **Preserve User Medium:** When the image explicitly suggests a medium (e.g. \"photo of\", \"photograph of\", \"illustration of\", \"painting of\", \"sketch of\", \"3D render of\"), honor it in the description. Do not pivot to a different medium to avoid difficulty — match the observed intent.\n\n[User Task]\nNow, carefully look at the input image connected to you. Follow the [System Roles & Rules] above to analyze the image, and then output only the final single expanded prompt paragraph. Do not include headers, bold labels like \"**Final Prompt:**\", or introductory phrases. Start directly with the prompt text itself."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "id": 89, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "字符串（多行）- 系统提示词 - 英文", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.26.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 12}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "links": [2498], "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "STRING"}], "size": [344.0996398925781, 292.5361633300781], "pos": [4461.3955078125, -725.9762573242188], "widgets_values": ["You are an expert prompt engineer for text-to-image models. Analyze the attached image and write a highly effective image-generation prompt paragraph in Chinese (中文) that accurately describes it.\n\nYou must follow this exact output format: Start your response with the word \"一张\" or \"一个\" and immediately continue the description in Chinese. Do not include any headers, tags, titles, intro text, or English explanations.\n\nStrictly follow these rules:\n1. Language: The final output prompt must be written entirely in Chinese (中文).\n2. Faithfulness First: Preserve all original subjects, actions, colors, spatial relationships, and details observed in the image. Do not add new objects, props, characters, or animals unless they are clearly present.\n3. Practical T2I Structure: Write a prompt that a text-to-image model can parse cleanly. Group subjects with their own attributes and actions. Use grounded phrasing for poses, interactions, and spatial layout.\n4. Style Planning Stays Internal: Use your internal reasoning to choose style, medium, framing, and lighting based on the image. Do not emit planning tags or wrappers.\n5. Text Rendering: If the image contains visible text, quotes, labels, or typography, specify the exact text clearly and wrap requested words in quotes.\n6. Avoid Over-Specification: Do not invent highly specific clothing, colors, materials, or scene details that are not clearly observable in the image.\n7. Structure: Write one single cohesive paragraph in Chinese. No bullets, JSON, or markdown formatting. \n8. Respect Existing Detail: If the image is already complex and detailed, lightly polish and finalize the description rather than heavily expanding — preserve the observed direction.\n9. Respect the Human Form: Treat depictions of people with dignity. Assume clothing covers genitals and intimate anatomy.\n10. Preserve User Medium: When the image explicitly suggests a medium (e.g. photo, illustration, painting, sketch), honor it and translate the medium accurately into Chinese (e.g., “一张...的照片”, “一幅...的插画”)."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "id": 261, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "字符串（多行）- 系统提示词 - 中文", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.26.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connec